Skip the jump event when nothing is listening.

LivingEntity's jump path built a CraftEntity handle and an EntityJumpEvent on every jump. The
event's only power is to veto the jump, so with no listener registered it always returns true and
the jump happens regardless.

Mobs jump constantly while pathfinding - over blocks, up slabs, out of water - so this runs far
more often than the name suggests.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
@@ -3907,1 +3907,3 @@
-                        if (new EntityJumpEvent(getBukkitLivingEntity()).callEvent()) {
+                        if (EntityJumpEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0
+                            || new EntityJumpEvent(getBukkitLivingEntity()).callEvent()) {
                         this.jumpFromGround();
